.TH GIT-STAGE-BATCH-INSTALL-ASSETS 1 "May 2026" "git-stage-batch @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-stage-batch-install-assets \- install bundled assistant assets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-stage-batch install-assets
[\fBclaude-agents\fR|\fBclaude-skills\fR|\fBcodex-skills\fR]
[\fB\-\-filter\fR \fIPATTERN\fR...]
[\fB\-\-global\fR]
[\fB\-\-force\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B install-assets
installs bundled assistant assets into the current repository.
With
.BR \-\-global ,
install into the user's home directory instead. A global install does not
require a Git repository.
.TP
.B claude-agents
Install into
.BR .claude/agents/ .
.TP
.B claude-skills
Install into
.BR .claude/skills/ .
Required bundled Claude agents for those skills are installed too.
.TP
.B codex-skills
Install into
.BR .agents/skills/ .
The shared internal drafter brief is written to
.BR .agents/internal/commit-message-drafter.md .
.PP
All groups include a default contribution guide under
.B .claude/internal/CONTRIBUTING.md
or
.BR .agents/internal/CONTRIBUTING.md .
Skills use it only when the target project has no CONTRIBUTING.md.
Project instructions and hooks take precedence. Installation never creates
or replaces the project's CONTRIBUTING.md.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I GROUP
Install only one bundled asset group. If omitted, install every group.
.TP
.BI "\-\-filter " PATTERN "..."
Install only bundled assets whose entry names match gitignore-style patterns.
.TP
.B \-\-global
Install skills and their companions under
.BR ~/.claude/skills/ ,
.BR ~/.claude/agents/ ,
and
.BR ~/.agents/skills/ .
Internal resources go under the corresponding ~/.claude/internal/ or
~/.agents/internal/ directory. Global installs do not create or modify
Codex configuration, including sandbox settings, even with --force.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite an existing installed asset.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-stage-batch (1)
